Description: Web frontend rules and patterns
Globs: frontend-web/**/*

# Web Frontend Rules - Clean Scapes P4P System

## Component Structure
- Use functional components with hooks
- Separate container and presentational components when needed
- Use React Context for global state (auth, theme)
- Keep components focused and reusable

## Layout Pattern
- Use layout components: `AdminLayout`, `ManagerLayout`, `ForemanLayout`
- Layouts include: Sidebar navigation, Top navbar, Main content area
- Route-based layouts in `App.js`

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Create reusable component classes when needed
- Follow mobile-first responsive design
- Maintain consistent spacing and colors

## State Management
- Use React Context API for:
  - Authentication state (`AuthContext`)
  - User preferences
- Use local state (`useState`) for:
  - Form inputs
  - Component-specific UI state
- Use `useEffect` for data fetching

## API Integration
- Use `services/api.js` for all API calls
- Include authentication token in headers
- Handle loading states
- Display error messages to users
- Use try-catch for error handling

## Form Handling
- Validate inputs before submission
- Show validation errors inline
- Disable submit button during submission
- Show success/error messages after submission

## Routing
- Use React Router DOM
- Protect routes with authentication checks
- Redirect based on user role after login
- Use route parameters for dynamic pages

## Charts and Visualizations
- Use Chart.js with react-chartjs-2
- Make charts responsive
- Use consistent color schemes
- Include legends and labels
- Show loading states while fetching data

## Data Tables
- Use consistent table styling
- Include sorting and filtering
- Show loading states
- Handle empty states (no data)
- Make rows clickable for details

## Error Handling
- Use ErrorBoundary for React errors
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for debugging
- Provide retry options when appropriate

## Loading States
- Show loading spinners for async operations
- Use skeleton screens for better UX
- Disable buttons during submission
- Show progress indicators for long operations

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML
- Include ARIA labels where needed
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain color contrast ratios

## Performance
- Lazy load routes when possible
- Optimize images
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders

## Role-Based UI
- Show/hide features based on user role
- Admin: Full access to all features
- Manager: Analytics and reports only
- Foreman: Team management features only
